<title>INDIA: India's NSE declares three members as defaulters.</title>
<headline>India's NSE declares three members as defaulters.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Stock Exchange of India Ltd (NSE) said on Monday that it declared three members as defaulters on account of their failure to fulfil their obligations.</p>
<p>In a statement, the NSE identified the three members as Amit Financial Services Ltd., Balshia Securities Ltd., and Nego Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>It said there were no outstandings due to the market as there was a settlement guarantee.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
